{title: 181 - Does Jesus Care?}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #181 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 181}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C/G]Does Jesus care [Am/E]when my [C/E]heart is pained Too [Em]deeply for mirth or song,
[Em]As the burdens press, [G]and the cares distress And the way grows [G7]weary and long?
[C/G]Oh yes, He cares, [G]I know He [Am]cares, [C]His heart is touched [G7/D]with my grief;
[G]When the days are [G7]weary, the long nights dreary, [C/G]I [Em]know my [G]Savior cares.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C]O yes, He cares- [G]I know [Em]He cares!
[G7]His heart is touched [C/G]with my [G]grief;
[Am]When the days [C]are weary,
[C/G]The long nights [Am/E]dreary,
[C]I know my Savior cares. (He cares.)
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C/G]Does Jesus care when my way [Em]is dark
[Em]With a [G]nameless dread and [G7]fear?
[C/G]As the daylight [G]fades [Am]into [C]deep night [G7/D]shades,
[G]Does He [G7]care enough [C/G]to [G]be near?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C/G]Does Jesus care when [Em]I've said goodbye
[Em]To the [G]dearest on earth to [G7]me,
[C/G]And my sad heart [G]aches [Am]till [C]it nearly [G7]breaks '
[G]Is it [G7]aught to Him? [C/G]Does [G]He see?
{end_of_verse}
